<Text title="Privacy policy | thetoolproject" description="How thetoolproject handles files, contact emails, and basic website request data." heading="Privacy policy" lead="Your files stay on your device when you use our conversion tools." path="/privacy/">
  <h2>Files and tool input</h2>
  <p>The conversion tools process files and pasted text in your browser. We do not receive or store the files you choose, the text you paste, or the results you download. You do not need an account to use the tools.</p>

  <h2>Website requests</h2>
  <p>When your browser loads the site, the hosting provider receives information needed to serve it, which may include your IP address, browser details, and the pages requested. The site code does not include analytics trackers or set advertising cookies. Hosting providers may keep routine request and security logs under their own policies.</p>

  <h2>Messages you send</h2>
  <p>If you email <a href="mailto:hello@thetoolproject.com">hello@thetoolproject.com</a>, we receive your email address and whatever you include in your message. We use that information to read and respond to you and to address the issue you raised. Do not send sensitive files or personal information you do not want shared with us. You can ask us to delete your message by emailing the same address.</p>

  <h2>GitHub</h2>
  <p>If you visit the <a href="https://github.com/harshit-dixit/thetoolproject.com">repository</a> or post an issue, GitHub handles that visit and anything you submit there under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">its privacy statement</a>. Issues are public, so do not include private data in them.</p>

  <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy if the site changes. The current version will appear on this page. For questions about your data, email <a href="mailto:hello@thetoolproject.com">hello@thetoolproject.com</a>.</p>
</Text>
